<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Breuci</h1><p class="st-meta">200 BCE – 9 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Pannonian people of the lower Sava valley who led, and then betrayed, the great revolt against Rome of 6–9 CE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Breuci lived along the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sava">Sava</a> in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/serbia">Serbia</a>, among the Pannonian peoples of the region. They appear in Roman sources as Roman armies pushed into the Sava valley.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Known mainly from Roman accounts, they were a populous tribal people of farmers and stockbreeders, said to field large armies. In 6 CE, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> levied troops for a war against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/marcomanni">Marcomanni</a>, they rose under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bato-the-breucian">Bato the Breucian</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pinnes">Pinnes</a>, joining the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daesitiates">Daesitiates</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-illyrian-revolt">Great Illyrian Revolt</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 8 CE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bato-the-breucian">Bato the Breucian</a> surrendered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pinnes">Pinnes</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and was then executed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bato-the-daesitiate">Bato of the Daesitiates</a>. The Breuci submitted, and their young men were enrolled in Roman auxiliary units, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cohort">cohortes</a> Breucorum, that served across the empire.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 200 BCE – 9 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Balkans and Hungary</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:55.72%;width:4.16%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>200 BCE – 9 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Bato the Breucian, Pinnes</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Pannonian polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Pannonian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/croatia">Croatia</a>, <a href="/countries/serbia">Serbia</a>, <a href="/countries/bosnia-and-herzegovina">Bosnia and Herzegovina</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Pannonian Breuci</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-96&amp;focus=breuci" aria-label="Breuci on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5067 564 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Breuci lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5387 820h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5387 820h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Croatia. <a href="/atlas?year=-96&amp;focus=breuci">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

